  "worked_solution": "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-3x+4z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=\u27e8-3,0,4\u27e9.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+31=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=\u27e81,-2,0\u27e9.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =\u27e8-3,0,4\u27e9\\times \u27e81,-2,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =8i+4j+6k \\\\  & =\u27e88,4,6\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
